  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pushpa Chinnaraj vs The District Collector on 11 September, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No.1460 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 11.09.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No.14608 of 2024 and W.M.P. No. 15885 of 2024 1. Pushpa Chinnaraj 2. Karthiga ... Petiti Vs 1 . The District Collector, Coimbatore District, Coimbatore. 2. The Tahsildhar, Annur Taluk, Coimbatore District. 3. The Commissioner, Annur Panchayat Union, Annur & Post, Coimbatore District. 4. The President, Kattampatty Village Panchayat, Annur Panchayat Union, Kattampatty, Coimbatore District. 5. C.Hari Sankar ... Respond 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Pushpa Chinnaraj vs The District Collector on 11 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/112716306/ 1 Writ Petition is filed under Article 226 of the Consti praying to issue a Writ of Mandamus, directing the second to fourth respondents take appropriate action against the fifth respondent fo M/sA.A.Thirumana Mandapam at Sf No. 292/2B, Muthalipalayam Road, Kattampatti Panchayat, Annur Taluk, Coimbatore District without Fire Safety License, Food Safety certificate and S certificate. For Petitioner : Mr. S.Kamadevan For Respondents : Mr. N.Naveen Kumar, Government Advocate (for R1 & R2 Mr. G.Krishnaraja, Additional Government Pleader (for R3 & R4) Mr. Kingsly Solomon (for R5) 4. While that being so, the first petitioner's husband died on 10.06.2023. However, the fifth respondent, on his own and without obtaining any necessary licence or safety measures, runs the Marriage Hall, which was originally licensed in favour of the first p e t i t i o n e r ' s h u s b a n d . C o n s e q u e n t l y , t h e p e t i t i o n e r s l o d g e d a c o m p l a i n t .",
    "facts": "3. The first petitioner is the wife of Chinnaraj, the second petitioner is her daughter. The fifth respondent is the son of the first petitioner. During his lifetime, the first petitioner's husband, viz., the said Chinnaraj, was the sole proprietor of M/s A.A. Thirumana Mandapam situated at S.F No. 292/2B, Ganesapuram, Muthalipalayam Road, Kattampatti Panchayat, Annur Taluk, Coimbatore District. After his demise, the entire property owned by the first petitioner's husband devolved upon the petitioners and the fifth respondent.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
